Subject: [PATCH 30/36] Zeroize stack memory in ML-KEM operations

This introduces the FIPS_ZEROIZE_STACK macro to allocate and cleanse a large
block of stack memory, ensuring that intermediate values left by previously
called functions are securely erased. The macro is applied to ML-KEM key
generation, encapsulation, and decapsulation functions. This change guarantees
that internal computations do not leave sensitive data on the stack,
fulfilling FIPS 203 requirements for the ML-KEM implementation.

Signed-off-by: Simo Sorce <simo@redhat.com>
---
